  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Orange Corners: OC Funding Connect</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Access to finance remains one of the main challenges for young entrepreneurs across Africa. While many Orange Corners alumni have promising businesses, they often struggle to find the right investors, prepare funding documents, or navigate complex application processes. This limits their ability to grow and scale their enterprises. To address this, the Orange Corners team at the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) has partnered with Vula, a South African digital innovation company, to pilot the Vula Funding Assistant &#x2013; an AI-powered tool that helps entrepreneurs identify relevant funding opportunities and generate tailored application documents. The project builds on RVO&#x2019;s broader Private Sector Development (PSD) agenda to test innovative digital solutions that can make access to finance more inclusive and efficient. During the six-month pilot, around 40 Orange Corners alumni from different countries will be onboarded and supported to use the tool. Their experiences will inform improvements and assess the potential for wider rollout across the Orange Corners network. By combining AI technology with local entrepreneurship support, this pilot aims to reduce information gaps, save time, and improve the quality of funding applications, helping more young entrepreneurs secure the capital they need to grow their businesses. The project also supports funders by onboarding them onto the platform and by supporting them to efficiently manage deal flow, so that they spend less time searching for fitting investment-ready entrepreneurs.</narrative>
  </description>
